fact PwaInstallabilityCriteria {
  id: "@community/fact-pwa-installability-criteria"
  version: "1.0.0"

  domain: frontend-design

  description: "A browser install prompt appears only when all four installability criteria are simultaneously met: served over HTTPS, has a registered service worker with a fetch handler, has a manifest with name/icons/start_url/display, and is not already installed."

  statement: """
    PWA install prompt (beforeinstallprompt / Chrome install button) fires only when ALL four are true:
    1. HTTPS (or localhost for development) — plain HTTP never triggers the prompt.
    2. Service worker registered and active with a fetch event handler — empty SW is insufficient.
    3. Web app manifest linked in <head> with required fields:
       - name (or short_name)
       - icons: at least one 192×192px and one 512×512px PNG/WebP
       - start_url
       - display: "standalone" | "fullscreen" | "minimal-ui"
    4. The app is not already installed on the device.

    Failing any single criterion silently prevents the prompt — no error is thrown.
    Lighthouse PWA audit reports each criterion independently.
  """

  source: [
    "github.com/ehmo/platform-design-skills, skills/web/SKILL.md §11.4 (MIT)",
    "https://web.dev/install-criteria/",
  ]

  notes: [
    "The 192px icon is used in Android home screen; 512px is used in splash screens and store listings.",
    "short_name (≤12 chars) is displayed under the home screen icon; name is used in install dialogs.",
    "iOS Safari uses its own Add to Home Screen flow and does not support beforeinstallprompt — show an in-app iOS install prompt using custom UI when navigator.standalone === false.",
  ]

  related: [
    @community/rule-pwa-web-app-manifest,
    @community/fact-pwa-display-mode-taxonomy,
    @community/pattern-pwa-service-worker-offline,
  ]
}
